{"$message_type":"diagnostic","message":"expected a type, found a trait","code":{"code":"E0782","explanation":"Trait objects must include the `dyn` keyword.\n\nErroneous code example:\n\n```edition2021,compile_fail,E0782\ntrait Foo {}\nfn test(arg: Box<Foo>) {} // error!\n```\n\nTrait objects are a way to call methods on types that are not known until\nruntime but conform to some trait.\n\nTrait objects should be formed with `Box<dyn Foo>`, but in the code above\n`dyn` is left off.\n\nThis makes it harder to see that `arg` is a trait object and not a\nsimply a heap allocated type called `Foo`.\n\nTo fix this issue, add `dyn` before the trait name.\n\n```edition2021\ntrait Foo {}\nfn test(arg: Box<dyn Foo>) {} // ok!\n```\n\nThis used to be allowed before edition 2021, but is now an error.\n"},"level":"error","spans":[{"file_name":"src\\..\\src\\main\\java\\io\\legado\\app\\adapters\\ReaderAdapterInterface.rs","byte_start":904,"byte_end":912,"line_start":31,"line_end":31,"column_start":28,"column_end":36,"is_primary":true,"text":[{"text":"        debug_log: Option<&DebugLog>,","highlight_start":28,"highlight_end":36}],"label":null,"suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null}],"children":[{"message":"you can add the `dyn` keyword if you want a trait object","code":null,"level":"help","spans":[{"file_name":"src\\..\\src\\main\\java\\io\\legado\\app\\adapters\\ReaderAdapterInterface.rs","byte_start":904,"byte_end":904,"line_start":31,"line_end":31,"column_start":28,"column_end":28,"is_primary":true,"text":[{"text":"        debug_log: Option<&DebugLog>,","highlight_start":28,"highlight_end":28}],"label":null,"suggested_replacement":"dyn ","suggestion_applicability":"MachineApplicable","expansion":null}],"children":[],"rendered":null}],"rendered":"\u001b[1m\u001b[91merror[E0782]\u001b[0m\u001b[1m\u001b[97m: expected a type, found a trait\u001b[0m\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[96m--> \u001b[0msrc\\..\\src\\main\\java\\io\\legado\\app\\adapters\\Reade